<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills sold out, yield 17.48 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills sold out, yield 17.48 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 1.0 billion levs of four-week discount T-bills was sold out, yielding 17.48 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>Five financial institutions took part in the auction, the BNB said.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3010497009</p>
<p> Auction date		     January 10, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date			 January 16, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		    February 13, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    1.083 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		85.09 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    1.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     85.12 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    17.48 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
